Here is a draft of the main independent system claim, structured according to standard patent drafting conventions and incorporating reference numerals.

***

**1.** A display system (100) comprising:
	a display device (102) configured to present visual content (104) to a user (106);
	an eye-tracking sensor (108) configured to capture eye movement data associated with the user (106); and
	at least one processor (110) communicatively coupled to the display device (102) and the eye-tracking sensor (108), the at least one processor (110) configured to:
		determine a current point of regard (POR) (112) of the user (106) relative to the display device (102) based on the eye movement data;
		define a first display region (114) centered on or encompassing the current POR (112);
		define a second display region (116) situated peripherally relative to the first display region (114);
		render the visual content (104) on the display device (102) such that the first display region (114) is rendered with a first set of image parameters (118) and the second display region (116) is rendered with a second set of image parameters (120), wherein the first set of image parameters (118) differs from the second set of image parameters (120);
		perform an image-based analysis on the visual content (104) to identify one or more visual saliency features (122);
		predict a future POR (124) of the user (106) based on a combination of the eye movement data and the identified one or more visual saliency features (122); and
		dynamically adjust at least one of the first display region (114) or the second display region (116) on the display device (102) in accordance with the predicted future POR (124) prior to the user's gaze reaching the predicted future POR (124).

***

### Key Strategic Highlights of this Draft:
* **Broad "Image Parameters" Scope:** Instead of limiting the distinction to just "resolution" or "foveated rendering," using "first set of image parameters" and "second set of image parameters" allows dependent claims to cover resolution, frame rate, color depth, anti-aliasing level, or lighting/shading complexity.
* **Image-Related Analysis:** Uses "visual saliency features" (e.g., high-contrast areas, moving objects, faces) to broadly capture content-aware/predictive tracking algorithms without locking into a specific machine-learning model.
* **Pre-emptive Shift:** The phrase *"prior to the user's gaze reaching the predicted future POR"* explicitly captures the latency-reduction benefit of predictive foveated rendering.
